 "description": "The Gladiator Mk IIF is a gift British fighter. It has been in the game since the start of the Open Beta Test prior to Update 1.27. This fighter aircraft used to be a part of Britain's reserve aircraft before it and the Gladiator Mk IIS were removed and replaced by the Fury and Nimrod aircraft. At Rank I and a battle rating of, this plane would typically have been one of the first fighters a new player will research. However, the Gladiator, like its sea-based cousin, may be difficult to seek success in, especially in Realistic Battles mode. Within RB, when up-tiering comes into play, it will have to deal with not only biplane adversaries such as the CR.42 , F3F-2 and the very manoeuvrable Ki-10 , but also more advanced fighters such as the P-40E , Bf 109s , I-16s , and Ki-43s . All these plane types have several varying advantages against the Gladiator, which can make early grinding a bit unbearable for some players.",
